00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:29.490
when would a student be at which school
and how many units would they be taking?

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:31.560
&gt;&gt; Sure.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:36.190
So let me start by focusing my answer
towards people that are not yet

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:37.570
enrolled in either program.

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:40.280
So this would be for brand new people.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:43.470
You can start with either program.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:45.360
If you start at the GSB,

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.280
your first year you would be primarily be
taking GSB coursework.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.350
So MBA courses.

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:52.920
And would probably have room for

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:57.040
about one to three Electrical Engineering
courses if you desire to take them.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:58.280
And then your second and

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:02.350
third years would be a blend of Electrical
Engineering and MBA courses.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.810
And you could choose what blend you wanted
to do.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:10.360
So you could primarily in one quarter be
heavy on Electrical Engineering or

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:12.170
heavy on MBA coursework.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:14.400
So there's a lot of flexibility.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:17.755
If you were to start at the Electrical
Engineering program,

00:08:17.755 --> 00:08:22.646
you would spend your first year primarily
focused on Electrical Engineering courses.

00:08:22.646 --> 00:08:27.545
And if you wished, you could probably take
a small number of GSB electives.

00:08:27.545 --> 00:08:32.570
And then your second year, you would be
almost completely at the GSB.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:35.830
And again, you would have that option to
take maybe one to three

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:38.220
courses in Electrical Engineering and

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:42.830
then your third year would be a blend of
electrical engineering and MBA courses.

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:50.351
So overall, as far as units this joint
degree requires 84 GSB units.

00:08:50.351 --> 00:08:57.514
And 45 MS units in Electrical Engineering
for a total of 129.

00:08:57.514 --> 00:09:00.961
And the number of units you're going to
take per quarter is really going to

00:09:00.961 --> 00:09:04.350
vary depending on what program you're
leaning more heavily into.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:07.692
So at the GSB, students tend to take a
higher course load.

00:09:07.692 --> 00:09:12.349
And over at Electrical Engineering, the
students tend to take a lower number of

00:09:12.349 --> 00:09:15.434
units per quarter, just due to the
technical nature and

00:09:15.434 --> 00:09:18.930
hours required outside of the classroom to
complete the work.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:22.731
But we are pretty confident that students
should be able to

00:09:22.731 --> 00:09:25.756
complete the full joint degree in nine
quarters.

00:09:25.756 --> 00:09:31.142
&gt;&gt; And so, if GSB students averages 18
units a quarter, what would you say,

00:09:31.142 --> 00:09:34.010
