deadlines and

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:46.380
I'll just say that for School of
Engineering there's one deadline,

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.160
which I believe is December 15th.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:49.490
Is that right, Katy?

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:50.200
&gt;&gt; December 9th.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:50.950
&gt;&gt; December 9th.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.870
Okay.
December 9th 2014.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:54.730
So one deadline.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:59.130
Now what makes it a little complicated is
for the business school,

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:05.030
there are three deadlines that you have to
choose from.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:10.880
So you can apply in October or January or
April.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:16.096
We would suggest, however, that if you're
applying to the joint degree and

00:12:16.096 --> 00:12:18.987
you are not currently a Stanford student,

00:12:18.987 --> 00:12:23.339
we would highly encourage you to apply in
the second round.

00:12:23.339 --> 00:12:29.552
And the reason for that is that you know,
you could apply in the first round but

00:12:29.552 --> 00:12:34.832
you wouldn't know yet you wouldn't get
your decision back from

00:12:34.832 --> 00:12:40.566
Electrical Engineering before the deadline
to respond to your MBA offer.

00:12:40.566 --> 00:12:46.520
And conversely you can apply in the third
round but you wouldn't

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:52.870
know your GSB offer before you had to
reply to School of Engineering's offer.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:57.880
So if you want complete information and
know if you got into both schools in order

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:03.810
to make your decision to come to Stanford,
the best round for you would be round two.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:08.070
Now if you're a current Master's in
Engineering School student,

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:11.170
then you could really apply in any round.

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:11.670
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:14.500
&gt;&gt; So any, any of those three rounds.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:22.730
For the business school the application
requirements are as follows.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.280
We require a transcript.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:30.060
We do require the the standardized test.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:34.180
But again, if you're applying to the Joint
Degree Program,

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:37.760
you would want to take the GRE and not the
GMAT.

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:41.540
Because the School of Engineering does not
accept the GMAT.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:46.160
So if you're looking at the joint degree,
please save yourself some time and

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.720
take only the GRE.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.910
If you are an international student and

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:58.110
you went to school where the language of
instruction was not English,

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:02.340
then you do need to take one of the
English language tests.

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:07.610
But again School of Engineering will only
accept the TOEFL.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:12.640
So if you're applying to the Joint Degree
Program again, save yourself some time and

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:13.730
just take the TOEFL.

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:17.780
Although the Business School will accept
some of the other English language tests.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:24.240
We also at the Business School require two
recommendations.

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:30.590
And your first recommendation must come
from a current direct

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:35.310
supervisor at work, and if you don't have

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:39.890
work experience that could be from an
internship or a summer job.

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:41.580
Your second letter of reference,

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:46.060
you have a choice of either choosing
another supervisor.

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:50.770
If we scroll down here, you can see, you
can chose another supervisor or

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:52.490
you can chose a peer.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:57.330
Which is a person who's worked, you know,
on a, on a team with you.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:02.430
The work experience I wanna mention.

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:06.310
We do not require work experience to,

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:10.350
to come to Stanford in the, in the
Business School.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:14.630
So you can apply as a college senior and

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:20.040
if you are admitted, you actually have the
luxury of, of

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:23.750
being able to decide if you want to come
immediately after you graduate college.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:29.370
Or we do offer deferrals to college
seniors of one or two or three years.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:34.420
We also ask you about extracurricular
activities, if you have them.

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:38.620
And lastly, there's two essay questions.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:44.250
What matters most to you and why, and why
Stanford?

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:47.000
Katy, what about for

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:50.960
Engineering, can you please walk us
through the application requirements?

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:52.890
&gt;&gt; Sure, so for EE,

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:57.400
we have an annual admissions process with
one deadline, as Allison mentioned.

00:15:57.400 --> 00:16:00.730
This year that deadline will be December
9th.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:03.705
And students that are applying during the
annual process,

00:16:03.705 --> 00:16:05.863
they are admitted to start in autumn
quarter.

00:16:05.863 --> 00:16:10.258
So students that meet that December 9th
deadline will be applying for

00:16:10.258 --> 00:16:13.317
admission to start in September 2015.

00:16:13.317 --> 00:16:15.950
Again no work experience is required.

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:19.460
Many of our students do have some work
experience any where

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:23.120
from one to four years usually on average.

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:27.400
To be eligible to apply to the MS in
Electrical Engineering,

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:32.570
students must hold a four years bachelors
degree from a credited institution and

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:34.950
that's a requirement from Stanford.

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:39.130
Almost all of our students that are
admitted do come from a STEM,

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:43.850
science, technology, engineering, or math
or hard sciences background.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.210
Although it is not required.

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:49.700
There are also no prerequisites in terms
of specific classes.

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:54.670
But our students do need to have a very
strong foundation in engineering and

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:58.390
specifically in electrical engineering is
strongly recommended.

00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:01.470
Because this is a rigorous academic
program, your application should

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:07.210
really showcase your propensity for
graduate level study in EE at Stanford.

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:11.350
So you'll find a list of all of our
application requirements on our website.

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:14.040
And I'm not gonna go through each of the
individual requirements.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:16.373
But there are a few that I do wanna
highlight.

00:17:16.373 --> 00:17:18.429
Specifically the GPA and GRE, so

00:17:18.429 --> 00:17:23.653
one of our most frequently asked questions
is, is there a minimum for the GPA or GRE?

00:17:23.653 --> 00:17:28.940
No, there is no minimum, typically our
students that are admitted tend

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:33.185
to be in the top ranks of their
undergraduate classes, and

00:17:33.185 --> 00:17:36.615
then also in the top percentile of the
GRE.

00:17:36.615 --> 00:17:41.055
We don't have an average in terms of our
admitted students for the GRE,

00:17:41.055 --> 00:17:45.865
however typically our successful
applicants are in the 90th percentile or

00:17:45.865 --> 00:17:48.833
higher on the quantitative section of the
GRE.

00:17:48.833 --> 00:17:52.405
Again, that's not an average, it's not a
minimum or a requirement,

00:17:52.405 --> 00:17:56.171
it's just something that we typically see
in our successful applicants.

00:17:56.171 --> 00:17:59.710
Also wanted to discuss the letter of
recommendation.

00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:03.800
So we require a minimum and maximum of
three letters of recommendation.

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:08.290
